UID:f2ade82260af42735122b328@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260907T180731Z
SUMMARY:BEN SCHMIDT-SWARTZ QUARTET
LOCATION:Merrimans’ Playhouse | 401 E. Colfax Ave.\, Suite 135 | South Be
 nd\, IN 46617
DESCRIPTION:The Ben Schmidt-Swartz Quartet explores original music as well 
 as some choice jazz standards that are meaningful to the band and fun to 
 play. The aesthetic comes out of a tradition of decades of reference poin
 ts from the great saxophone quartets from jazz history. From Coleman Hawk
 ins\, to John Coltrane\; from Lester Young and Oscar Peterson to Dexter G
 ordon\, this group hopes to honor\, and continue in that legacy.\n\nBen S
 chmidt-Swartz - saxophone\n\nMatthew Fries - piano\n\nCarlo De Rosa - bas
 s\n\nNelson Oliva - drums\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/ev
 ents/ben-schmidt-swartz-quartet/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/ben-schmidt-swartz-quartet/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260909T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260909T210000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:52a6dc87c9464bc73493b5b4@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260907T180731Z
SUMMARY:EXHIBITION OPENING | MELI BANDERA: “GENERATION GAPS: ODES TO FAMI
 LIAL MEMORIES.”
LOCATION:IU South Bend Civil Rights Heritage Center | 1040 W. Washington | 
 South Bend\, IN 46601
DESCRIPTION:Meli Bandera (they/them) crafts soft altars built from paper\, 
 felt\, and wool to capture the memories of those who came before them: th
 e scent of their grandmother’s garden after she waters it\, the rhythmi
 c thump of a lawnmower on a summer afternoon\, or the shared sweetness of
  bolis enjoyed with loved ones. Bandera builds these memories into tangib
 le forms\, acknowledging the gaps and absences that shape our understandi
 ng of family history.\n\nBandera’s fiber-based artworks are devotional 
 gestures\, mirroring the way memories shift and transform over time. Imag
 ine a watermelon lemonade that will never be made by an abuela again\, or
  a bisabuela walking to the centro for water. These are the threads Bande
 ra pulls from\, using recycled pulp\, cochineal dye\, and wool to create 
 pieces that feel both ancient and present. These works are a form of time
  travel\, using softness and humor to stretch grief and joy across eras.\
 n\n“Generation Gaps” opens with an evening event at the Civil Rights 
 Heritage Center on Thursday\, September 10\, 2026\, from 6:00 – 7:30 PM
 . Light refreshments will be served as you experience Bandera’s deeply 
 moving work. The exhibit remains on view through December 10 during the C
 enter's public hours.\n\nDetails at crhc.iusb.edu.\n\nMore Info: https://
 www.visitsouthbend.com/events/exhibition-opening-meli-bandera-generation-
 gaps-odes-to-familial-memories/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/exhibition-opening-meli-bandera-g
 eneration-gaps-odes-to-familial-memories/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260910T193000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
