BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fe3984b4c6f3c2c919b2e862@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260907T180731Z
SUMMARY:ROGER DALTREY
LOCATION:Four Winds Casino New Buffalo | 11111 Wilson Rd | NEW BUFFALO\, 49
 117
DESCRIPTION:Inducted into the Rock and Hall of Fame with The Who in 1990\, 
 Daltrey received a Lifetime Achievement award from the Grammy Foundation 
 along with the band in 2001. Daltrey and The Who co-founder Pete Townshen
 d received Kennedy Center Honors in 2008. Considered to have one of the m
 ost recognizable singing voices of all time\, Planet Rock listeners voted
  Daltrey Rock’s fifth-greatest voice in music history. He also received
  stellar reviews for his unique 2018 autobiography\, Thanks a Lot Mr. Kib
 blewhite\, with one critic describing it as how ‘the punk became rock
 ’s Godfather…’ Known for his magnetic presence and rebellious creat
 ive spirit\, Daltrey has also been an actor and film producer\, with mult
 iple roles in films\, theatre\, and television.\n\nHe’s released ten so
 lo studio albums\, including the acclaimed discs Daltrey\, Ride a Rock Ho
 rse\, One of the Boys \, and the 2018 release As Long As I Have You\, and
  such hit singles as “I’m Free\,” “Giving It All Away\,” “Wit
 hout Your Love\,” “Free Me” and “After the Fire.” His solo work
  has been compiled into two anthologies\, Martyrs and Madmen (1997) and M
 oonlighting (2005). Queen Elizabeth awarded him a CBE for his service to 
 music and charity in 2004.\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/e
 vents/roger-daltrey/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/roger-daltrey/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T213000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
