SUMMARY:UNITED 93 (2006)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Paul Greengrass With Christian Clemenson\, Klahid A
 bdalla\, J. J. Johnson Rated R\, 111 minutes\, DCP In English and Arabic 
 with English subtitles Released five years after the events on September 
 11\, 2001\, United 93 was a film largely supported by the families of the
  people depicted in the film and\, further\, received largely positive cr
 itical responses\, including a Best Director Oscar nomination for Paul Gr
 eengrass. Now twenty years after its release and on the 25th anniversary 
 of the tragedies\, revisiting this film that utilizes a real-time framing
  device to bring audiences into the world of a doomed flight is a good ex
 ercise both for remembering the people indelibly impacted by 9-11 and als
 o understanding how films and television continue to shape a world's memo
 ries and opinions of that day. Sponsored by the Meg and John P. Brogan En
 dowment for Classic Cinema.\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/
 events/united-93-2006/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/united-93-2006/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T203000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
